# Kitchen room (ticket 28.7): the backdrop of the kitchen level, the room round the island's worktop at 60 times life size. The origin is the worktop's surface centre, so the level
# places it at (0, 0, 0): the floor (grey slate) is at y = -55 and the ceiling (cream, with the walls) at y = 101; the room inside is 300 (x) x 156 (y) x 270 (z), walls 3 m thick
# outside it. North (+z): a run of sage cabinets with an oak worktop at y = 0, white metro tiles to 36 m above it, a 72 x 72 m sash window (daylight, a basil pot on the sill)
# and upper cabinets either side. West and east: the same run with upper cabinets and warm light strips under them. South: a tall cream fridge with magnets and the door.
# Two brass pendant lamps hang over the island, their shades 65 m above the worktop. Eight materials: kitchen_wall, _slate, _tile, _cabinet, _oak, _brass, _glow, _basil.
# Emission: the window, the strips and the lamps' undersides are kitchen_glow, a pale warm material with emission 1 (30.1): it glows flat, in shadow too.
# No collider: the room is out of reach and takes no shadows.
# Plain big faces on purpose (no noise); the grid is coarse (about 1.2 m cells), so nothing thinner than 2 m is modelled.
format 1
collider none

